{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The Sidonians call Hermon, etc.</b> And elsewhere it says (Deuteronomy 4), ״וְעַד הַר שִּׂיאֹן הוּא חֶרְמוֹן״ — see, it has four names. Why was it necessary to write them? To tell the praise of the land of Israel — that four kingdoms gloried in it: this one saying, it shall be called by my name, and that one saying, it shall be called by my name." "<b>Snir.</b> It is snow in Ashkenaz language and in Canaanite language."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:47.030096088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}